# What this teaches / copy this pattern:
# Committed, NON-secret Vite build-time config for the DEPLOYED build (`vite build`
# runs in `production` mode, so Vite reads THIS file). Pairs with the Worker
# `env.production` var `PERSISTENCE=local` (wrangler.jsonc).
#
# `VITE_PERSISTENCE=local` selects the browser `localStorage` reservation store:
# the deployed Worker binds NO D1 and persists NOTHING server-side, so reservations
# live only in the staff browser. This MUST match the Worker `PERSISTENCE` var - a
# mismatch makes the browser call `/api/reservations` and hit the structured 501.
VITE_PERSISTENCE=local

# DEV-TEST-ONLY cell targeting is CLEARED here, explicitly, and the empty values are
# load-bearing. Vite loads `.env` FIRST for every mode and then layers this file on
# top, so leaving a key out does NOT give you a prod-only build: it inherits
# whatever `.env` has. An earlier version of this comment claimed absence made the
# deployed build "prod-only (byte-unchanged)", and that was false. A developer
# uncommenting `VITE_CHECKTIV_DEV_CELL=us` in `.env` for local testing silently
# shipped a public demo that sent LIVE publishable keys to the dev cell and got 403s
# on `/sdk/v1/working-token`.
#
# These pins also beat `.env.local`, which is where a developer's own non-production
# origins belong. Vite ranks a MODE-SPECIFIC file above a generic one, so
# `.env.production` wins over `.env.local` for a production build:
# https://vite.dev/guide/env-and-mode - "An env file for a specific mode (e.g.
# `.env.production`) will take higher priority than a generic one (e.g. `.env`)."
# Only `.env.production.local` (also gitignored) or a process env var outranks these.
#
# An empty flag is read as "no dev cell" (`resolveDevCellOrigin` in
# `src/shared/dev-cell.ts` returns null for a blank flag), so these lines pin prod
# behavior no matter what `.env` or `.env.local` says. The two origin variables are
# pinned empty as well so no non-production hostname can be inlined into the
# deployed bundle even if the flag were somehow set. Do not delete any of them to
# "clean up".
VITE_CHECKTIV_DEV_CELL=
VITE_CHECKTIV_DEV_CELL_SDK_API_BASE=
VITE_CHECKTIV_DEV_CELL_WORKSPACE_BASE_URL=

# Do NOT edit the pins above to run a dev-cell deploy. `pnpm run deploy` gates on
# `scripts/assert-no-dev-cell-in-deploy.mjs`, which reads the RESOLVED Vite env, the
# built client bundle, and the generated Worker deploy config, and fails on any
# dev-cell targeting in any of the three. Test against a non-production cell locally
# (`.env.local` + `.dev.vars`), never on the public demo.
